\title{scimapR accessor return-type stability contract}
\description{
scimapR treats the return type of its \strong{documented accessors} as a contract.
The column set (names and types) of an accessor's documented return value
will not change without a \href{https://lifecycle.r-lib.org/}{lifecycle}
deprecation and a corresponding \code{NEWS.md} entry. New columns may be \emph{added}
(a non-breaking change); existing documented columns will not be removed or
retyped silently.

This policy exists because a silent list -> tibble change in
\code{sm_coverage_breakdowns()} between 0.2.0 and 0.3.0 broke downstream code.
From 0.4.0, accessors that expose a tidy table take a \code{tidy = TRUE} argument
whose column set is the stable contract.
